abstract:
This document includes the progress reports on the following selected Regional Committee resolutions: Provide health
1. South-East Asia Regional Action Plan to implement Global Strategy to reduce harmful use of alcohol (2014–2025) (SEA/RC67/R4);
2. Ending preventable maternal, newborn and child mortality in the South-East Asia Region in line with the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and Global Strategy on women’s, children’s and adolescents’ health (SEA/RC69/R3);
3. Beginning of the Decade of Action for ending viral hepatitis, HIV and STIs as public health threats by 2030 in the South-East Asia Region (SEA/RC74(4)) and paragraph 31 of document (SEA/RC75/15);
4. Paro Declaration by the Health Ministers of Member States at the Seventy-fifth session of the WHO Regional Committee for South-East Asia on universal access to people-centered mental health care and services (SEA/RC75/R1);
5. (a) Monitoring progress and the acceleration plan for NCDs, including oral health and integrated eye care, in the South-East Asia Region (SEA/RC75/R2); (b) Extending and expanding the Regional Milestones of SEAHEARTS: an initiative to reduce CVD burden in the WHO South-East Asia Region (SEA/RC78(7)); and (c) Regional Action Plan and targets for prevention and control of noncommunicable diseases (2013–2020) (SEA/RC66/R6);
6. Enhancing social participation in support of primary health care and universal health coverage (SEA/RC75/R3);
7. Ministerial Declaration on adolescent-responsive health systems (SEA/RC77/R1)
8. Measles and rubella elimination with interruption of transmission of indigenous measles and rubella virus by 2026 (SEA/RC77/R3);
Protect health
9. Challenges in polio eradication (SEA/RC60/R8);
10. WHO South-East Asia Region Member States’ Declaration on collective response to COVID-19 (SEA/RC73/R1);
11. Expanding the corpus of the South-East Asia Regional Health Emergency Fund (SEARHEF) (SEA/RC77/R2); 
Promote health
12. Strategic Action Plan to reduce the double burden of malnutrition in the South-East Asia Region 2016–2025 (SEA/RC69/R5) 
The High-Level Preparatory Meeting for the Seventy-ninth Session of the WHO Regional Committee for South-East Asia, held in New Delhi, India on 11–12 August 2025, reviewed each progress report and made recommendations on them. The recommendations made by the HLP Meeting have been consolidated as Addendum 1 (SEA/RC79/14 Add. 1) to this Working Paper. 

A copy of each of the Regional Committee resolutions/decisions related to the above-mentioned progress reports is being submitted as Addendum 2 (SEA/RC79/14 Add. 2). 

In relation to sub-Agenda item 9.11, a Resource Mobilization Strategy for the South-East Asia Regional Health Emergency Funds (2026–2030) is submitted, for the information of the Regional Committee, as Addendum 3 (SEA/RC79/14 Add. 3). In relation to the sub-Agenda item 9.12, a detailed report (draft) presenting the final assessment of the implementation of the Resolution “Strategic Action Plan to reduce the double burden of Malnutrition in the South-East Asia Region 2016–2025 (SEA/RC69/R5)” is submitted, as an Addendum to the Working Paper on “Progress reports” (SEA/RC79/14 Add. 4). The final Working Papers along with four addenda are being presented to the Seventy-ninth Session of the WHO Regional Committee for South-East Asia for consideration and review, as appropriate.
